---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About GamesBrowse"
  description="Learn what GamesBrowse focuses on, how the portal is organized, and how native and embedded games fit into the site."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container stack">
      <div class="hero-panel stack">
        <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
        <h1>About GamesBrowse</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          GamesBrowse is a lightweight portal for free browser games, designed to help players find
          a game quickly and jump into play without extra setup.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="portal-info-grid">
        <section class="panel stack">
          <h2>What the site focuses on</h2>
          <p class="muted">
            GamesBrowse keeps the experience clean: game detail pages, category routes, simple
            discovery modules, and layouts that work well on desktop and mobile.
          </p>
          <p class="muted">
            The goal is not to bury players under heavy navigation or long explanations. The portal
            is built around quick discovery, fast loading, and easy replay.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="panel stack">
          <h2>How the catalog is structured</h2>
          <p class="muted">
            Each game has its own route, metadata, and category placement. Native mini-games and
            embedded iframe games share the same overall page structure so the site can grow without
            fragmenting the experience.
          </p>
          <p class="muted">
            Categories, featured sections, popular modules, and newest additions all come from one
            shared data source, which makes the portal easier to maintain as more games are added.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
